IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 11 -- Offences against public justice`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 201, 202, 203, 204, 204A, 204B, 205, 206, 207, 208, 210, 211,
-- 212, 213, 214, 215, 216, 216A, 216B, 217, 218, 219, 220, 221, 222, 223, 224, 225,
-- 225A, 225B, 225C, 228, 229.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The second half of Chapter 11, in six families. ss 201 to 204B are about EVIDENCE
-- AND INFORMATION: screening an offender by destroying evidence or lying (s 201),
-- omitting to inform (s 202), false information (s 203), destroying a document
-- (s 204), the general offence of perverting the course of justice (s 204A), and
-- bribing witnesses (s 204B). s 205 is personation in a suit. ss 206 to 210 are
-- FRAUD ON FORFEITURE, EXECUTION AND DECREES. s 211 is a false charge. ss 212 to
-- 216B are HARBOURING AND SCREENING OFFENDERS, with s 216B's meaning of "harbour".
-- ss 217 to 223 are PUBLIC SERVANTS who save offenders or property, or let prisoners
-- go; ss 224 to 225B are RESISTANCE, ESCAPE AND RESCUE; s 225C is the residual fine
-- for a prohibited act with no punishment provided; ss 228 and 229 are insulting a
-- public servant sitting judicially and personating an assessor.
--
-- Many of these sections grade punishment by the gravity of the offence concerned:
-- capital, life or 20 years, or less. Two facts carry that gravity for all of them,
-- and none of the gradings is decided.
--
-- The Explanations to ss 203, 212(2) and 216(2) make "offence" include an act
-- outside Singapore that would be punishable here under the listed sections (or,
-- for s 216, for which the person is liable to be apprehended here). They widen
-- what counts as an offence and add no limb.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED.

§§ `Sections 201 to 203 -- Screening an offender, omitting to inform, false information`

-- All three open on knowledge or reason to believe that an offence has been
-- committed. s 201 adds the intention of screening the offender and one of two acts:
-- making evidence disappear, or giving false information. s 203 is the same false
-- information WITHOUT the screening intention, so a s 201 lie is a s 203 lie too.
-- s 202 is the omission to give information one is legally bound to give.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 201"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes causing the disappearance of evidence or giving false information to screen an offender under Penal Code 1871 section 201
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed, and, intending to screen the offender from legal punishment, causing evidence of it to disappear or giving false information about it. The Illustration is helping a murderer hide the body.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes screening an offender by destroying evidence or false information` IF
        pj's `knows or has reason to believe that an offence has been committed`
    AND pj's `intends to screen the offender from legal punishment`
    AND (   pj's `causes evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear`
         OR pj's `gives information respecting that offence which he knows or believes to be false`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 202"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes intentional omission to give information of an offence by a person bound to inform under Penal Code 1871 section 202
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed, and intentionally omitting to give information about it which the person is legally bound to give.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes omission to give information of an offence` IF
        pj's `knows or has reason to believe that an offence has been committed`
    AND pj's `intentionally omits to give information respecting that offence which he is legally bound to give`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 203"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes giving false information respecting an offence committed under Penal Code 1871 section 203
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed, and giving information about it known or believed to be false. No screening intention is needed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes giving false information respecting an offence` IF
        pj's `knows or has reason to believe that an offence has been committed`
    AND pj's `gives information respecting that offence which he knows or believes to be false`

§§ `Sections 204 to 204B -- Destroying a document, perverting the course of justice, bribing witnesses`

-- s 204A's Explanation 1 takes a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted
-- for perjury OUT of the section, so it is a negated conjunct. Explanation 2 puts a
-- sentenced person's unlawful departure from Singapore to avoid serving the sentence
-- IN, as an act with the tendency, so it is a second route to the tendency fact.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 204"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes destruction of a document or electronic record to prevent its production as evidence under Penal Code 1871 section 204
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Secreting, destroying, obliterating or rendering illegible a document or electronic record the person may be lawfully compelled to produce as evidence before a court or a public servant, intending to prevent its production or use, or after being lawfully summoned or required to produce it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes destroying a document to prevent its production as evidence` IF
        pj's `secretes or destroys a document or electronic record which he may be lawfully compelled to produce as evidence before a court of justice or in a proceeding lawfully held before a public servant as such or obliterates or renders illegible the whole or any part of it`
    AND pj's `intends to prevent the document or electronic record from being produced or used as evidence before that court or public servant or does so after having been lawfully summoned or required to produce it for that purpose`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 204A Explanation 2"
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act has a tendency to obstruct the course of justice` IF
        pj's `does an act that has a tendency to obstruct prevent pervert or defeat the course of justice`
    OR  pj's `being sentenced to imprisonment leaves or attempts to leave Singapore unlawfully to avoid serving the sentence`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 204A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes obstructing, preventing, perverting or defeating the course of justice under Penal Code 1871 section 204A
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc An act with a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice -- including a sentenced person's unlawful departure to avoid the sentence -- done knowing it likely to have that effect or intending it. A mere warning to a witness that perjury is prosecutable is not enough.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes perverting the course of justice` IF
        `the act has a tendency to obstruct the course of justice` pj
    AND (   pj's `knows that the act is likely to obstruct prevent pervert or defeat the course of justice`
         OR pj's `intends to obstruct prevent pervert or defeat the course of justice`)
    AND NOT pj's `the act is a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 204B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes bribery of witnesses under Penal Code 1871 section 204B
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Giving, offering or procuring a gratification on an understanding that a person aware of a reportable offence will not report it, or that a witness will give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence; attempting to induce a witness to do so; or taking a benefit on an understanding that one will do so as a witness. A judicial proceeding is any in which evidence is or may be legally taken.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes bribery of a witness` IF
        pj's `gives confers or procures or promises or offers to give confer or procure or attempts to procure any gratification to upon or for any person upon an agreement or understanding that a person aware of an offence which any person is legally bound to give information respecting will abstain from reporting it to the police or an agency charged by law with investigating offences`
    OR  pj's `gives confers or procures or promises or offers to give confer or procure or attempts to procure any gratification to upon or for any person upon an agreement or understanding that a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding will give false testimony or withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`
    OR  pj's `attempts by any means to induce a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding to give false testimony or withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`
    OR  pj's `asks receives or obtains or agrees or attempts to receive or obtain any property or benefit for himself or any other person upon an agreement or understanding that a person will as a witness in a judicial proceeding give false testimony or withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`

§§ `Section 205 -- False personation in a suit or prosecution`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 205"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes false personation for the purpose of an act or proceeding in a suit or prosecution under Penal Code 1871 section 205
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Falsely personating another and in that character making an admission or statement, confessing judgment, causing process to issue, becoming bail or security, or doing any other act in a suit or criminal prosecution.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes false personation in a suit or prosecution` IF
        pj's `falsely personates another`
    AND pj's `in that assumed character makes an admission or statement or confesses judgment or causes process to be issued or becomes bail or security or does any other act in a suit or criminal prosecution`

§§ `Sections 206 to 210 -- Fraud on forfeiture, execution and decrees`

-- ss 206 and 207 share one intention -- to prevent property being taken as a
-- forfeiture, in satisfaction of a fine, in execution of a decree or order, or under
-- an enforcement order -- and differ in the act: removing or transferring the
-- property (s 206), or claiming it or deceiving about a right to it (s 207). ss 208
-- and 210 are the two sides of a fraudulent decree: suffering one against oneself
-- (s 208, the Illustration is a debtor letting a friend's collusive judgment share
-- in the proceeds) and obtaining one against another (s 210). "Fraudulently" in
-- these four is the s 25 term and comes from the `Fault` record, as it does in
-- ss 471 and 489F -- unlike s 477A's "with intent to defraud", which is not.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 206"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent its seizure under Penal Code 1871 section 206
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Removing, concealing, transferring or delivering property or an interest in it, intending to prevent it being taken as a forfeiture, in satisfaction of a fine, in execution of a decree or order, or under an enforcement order, made or likely to be made.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The removal must be fraudulent (s 25).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulent removal of property to prevent its seizure` pj f IF
        `the act is done fraudulently` f
    AND pj's `removes conceals transfers or delivers to any person any property or interest in property`
    AND pj's `intends thereby to prevent the property or interest from being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or which he knows to be likely to be pronounced by a court of justice or other competent authority or from being taken in execution of a decree or order or under or pursuant to an enforcement order made or which he knows to be likely to be made by a court of justice in a civil suit`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 207"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a fraudulent claim to property to prevent its seizure under Penal Code 1871 section 207
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Accepting, receiving or claiming property or an interest knowing one has no right to it, or practising deception about a right to it, with the same intention as s 206.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The claim must be fraudulent (s 25).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a fraudulent claim to property to prevent its seizure` pj f IF
        `the act is done fraudulently` f
    AND pj's `accepts receives or claims any property or interest in property knowing that he has no right or rightful claim to it or practises any deception touching any right to property or an interest in property`
    AND pj's `intends thereby to prevent the property or interest from being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or which he knows to be likely to be pronounced by a court of justice or other competent authority or from being taken in execution of a decree or order or under or pursuant to an enforcement order made or which he knows to be likely to be made by a court of justice in a civil suit`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 208"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulently suffering a decree for a sum not due under Penal Code 1871 section 208
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Causing or suffering a decree or order to pass against oneself for a sum not due, a larger sum, or property one's opponent is not entitled to, or to be executed after satisfaction.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The suffering of the decree must be fraudulent (s 25).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulently suffering a decree for a sum not due` pj f IF
        `the act is done fraudulently` f
    AND pj's `causes or suffers a decree or order to be passed against him at the suit of any person for a sum not due or for a larger sum than is due or for property or an interest in property to which that person is not entitled or causes or suffers a decree or order to be executed or enforced against him after it has been satisfied or for anything in respect of which it has been satisfied`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 210"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulently obtaining a decree for a sum not due under Penal Code 1871 section 210
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Obtaining a decree or order against another for a sum not due, a larger sum, or property one is not entitled to, or causing one to be executed after satisfaction, or suffering any such act in one's name.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The obtaining must be fraudulent (s 25).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulently obtaining a decree for a sum not due` pj f IF
        `the act is done fraudulently` f
    AND pj's `obtains a decree or order against any person for a sum not due or for a larger sum than is due or for property or an interest in property to which he is not entitled or causes a decree or order to be executed or enforced against any person after it has been satisfied or for anything in respect of which it has been satisfied or suffers or permits any such act to be done in his name`

§§ `Section 211 -- False charge of an offence with intent to injure`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 211"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a false charge of an offence made with intent to injure under Penal Code 1871 section 211
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc With intent to injure a person, instituting or causing a criminal proceeding against him or falsely charging him with an offence, knowing there is no just or lawful ground for it. A proceeding on a false charge of an offence punishable with death or 7 years or more goes to punishment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a false charge with intent to injure` IF
        pj's `intends to cause injury to a person`
    AND pj's `institutes or causes to be instituted a criminal proceeding against that person or falsely charges that person with having committed an offence`
    AND pj's `knows that there is no just or lawful ground for the proceeding or charge against that person`

§§ `Sections 212 to 216B -- Harbouring and screening offenders`

-- s 216B: "harbour" includes supplying shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms,
-- ammunition or means of conveyance, or assisting in any way to evade apprehension.
-- It governs ss 212, 216 and 216A and is a rule here so that the supply fact reaches
-- each harbouring limb.
--
-- s 212's Illustrations (b) and (c) are the pair that decides the intention element:
-- a spouse who gives food and shelter to a house-breaker with no intention to screen
-- him is not harbouring; a spouse who does so to help a gang-robber evade the police
-- before leaving Singapore is.
--
-- ss 213 and 214 are the two sides of a bargain to screen an offender: taking the
-- gratification (s 213) and giving it (s 214). Their Exception -- neither extends to
-- a case where the offence may lawfully be compounded -- is a negated conjunct on
-- both. s 215 is the recovery racket: taking a gratification for helping to recover
-- stolen movable property, unless all means are used to have the offender caught and
-- convicted.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 216B"
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person harbours the other within section 216B` IF
        pj's `harbours or conceals that person`
    OR  pj's `supplies the person with shelter food drink money clothes arms ammunition or means of conveyance or assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 212"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes harbouring an offender under Penal Code 1871 section 212
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc An offence having been committed, harbouring or concealing (in the s 216B sense) a person known or believed to be the offender, intending to screen him from legal punishment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes harbouring an offender` IF
        pj's `an offence has been committed`
    AND pj's `knows or has reason to believe that the person is the offender`
    AND `the person harbours the other within section 216B` pj
    AND pj's `intends to screen the offender from legal punishment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 213"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes taking a gift to screen an offender from punishment under Penal Code 1871 section 213
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Accepting, agreeing to accept or attempting to obtain a gratification or restitution of property in consideration of concealing an offence, screening a person from punishment, or not proceeding against him. Not where the offence may lawfully be compounded.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes taking a gift to screen an offender` IF
        pj's `accepts or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain any gratification for himself or any other person or any restitution of property to himself or any other person`
    AND pj's `in consideration of his concealing an offence or of his screening a person from legal punishment for an offence or of his not proceeding against a person for the purpose of bringing him to legal punishment`
    AND NOT pj's `the offence may lawfully be compounded`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 214"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes offering a gift or restoration of property in consideration of screening an offender under Penal Code 1871 section 214
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Giving, offering or agreeing to give a gratification or to restore property in consideration of the recipient concealing an offence, screening a person from punishment, or not proceeding against him. Not where the offence may lawfully be compounded.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes offering a gift to screen an offender` IF
        pj's `gives or causes or offers or agrees to give or cause any gratification to any person or to restore or cause the restoration of any property to any person`
    AND pj's `in consideration of that person concealing an offence or screening a person from legal punishment for an offence or not proceeding against a person for the purpose of bringing him to legal punishment`
    AND NOT pj's `the offence may lawfully be compounded`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 215"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes taking a gift to help recover stolen property under Penal Code 1871 section 215
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Taking or agreeing to take a gratification under pretence or on account of helping a person recover movable property lost through a Code offence, unless the person uses all means in his power to have the offender apprehended and convicted.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes taking a gift to help recover stolen property` IF
        pj's `takes or agrees or consents to take any gratification for himself or any other person under pretence or on account of helping a person to recover movable property of which he has been deprived by an offence punishable under this Code`
    AND NOT pj's `uses all means in his power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted of the offence`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 216"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes harbouring an offender who has escaped from custody or whose apprehension has been ordered under Penal Code 1871 section 216
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A person in lawful custody for an offence having escaped, or a public servant having lawfully ordered a person's apprehension for an offence; knowing of the escape or order; and harbouring or concealing (in the s 216B sense) that person intending to prevent his apprehension.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes harbouring an escapee or a person ordered to be apprehended` IF
        pj's `a person convicted of or charged with an offence and in lawful custody for it has escaped from that custody or a public servant in the exercise of his lawful powers has ordered a person to be apprehended for an offence`
    AND pj's `knows of the escape or of the order for apprehension`
    AND `the person harbours the other within section 216B` pj
    AND pj's `intends to prevent that person from being apprehended`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 216A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes harbouring robbers or gang-robbers under Penal Code 1871 section 216A
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Knowing or having reason to believe that persons are about to commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery, within or without Singapore, harbouring them (in the s 216B sense) intending to facilitate the robbery or screen them from punishment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes harbouring robbers` IF
        pj's `knows or has reason to believe that persons are about to commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery`
    AND (   pj's `harbours those persons or any of them`
         OR pj's `supplies the person with shelter food drink money clothes arms ammunition or means of conveyance or assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`)
    AND pj's `intends to facilitate the commission of the robbery or gang-robbery or to screen those persons or any of them from punishment`

§§ `Sections 217 to 223 -- Public servants saving offenders or property, and letting prisoners go`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 217"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant disobeying a direction of law to save a person from punishment or property from forfeiture under Penal Code 1871 section 217
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A public servant knowingly disobeying a direction of the law as to his conduct, intending or knowing it likely to save a person from punishment or reduce it, or to save property from forfeiture or a charge.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant disobeying the law to save a person or property` IF
        pj's `is a public servant`
    AND pj's `knowingly disobeys a direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as a public servant`
    AND pj's `intends thereby to save or knows it to be likely that he will thereby save a person from legal punishment or subject him to a lesser punishment than that to which he is liable or intends to save or knows that he is likely thereby to save property from forfeiture or a charge to which it is liable by law`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 218"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant framing an incorrect record to cause loss or save a person or property under Penal Code 1871 section 218
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A public servant charged with preparing a record or writing who frames it in a manner he knows to be incorrect, intending or knowing it likely to cause loss or injury to the public or any person, or to save a person from punishment or property from forfeiture.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant framing an incorrect record to save a person or property` IF
        pj's `is a public servant`
    AND pj's `is charged as a public servant with the preparation of a record or other writing`
    AND pj's `frames the record or writing in a manner which he knows to be incorrect`
    AND pj's `intends to cause or knows it to be likely that he will thereby cause loss or injury to the public or to any person or intends thereby to save or knows it to be likely that he will thereby save a person from legal punishment or intends to save or knows that he is likely thereby to save property from forfeiture or other charge to which it is liable by law`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 219"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant in a judicial proceeding making an order known to be contrary to law under Penal Code 1871 section 219
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A public servant who, corruptly or intending injury to any person, makes or pronounces in a judicial proceeding a report, order, verdict or decision he knows to be contrary to law.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant making a judicial order known to be contrary to law` IF
        pj's `is a public servant`
    AND pj's `corruptly or with intent to cause injury to any person makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding a report order verdict or decision which he knows to be contrary to law`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 220"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes commitment for trial or confinement by a person with authority who knows he is acting contrary to law under Penal Code 1871 section 220
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A person in an office giving legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement or to keep them confined, who corruptly or intending injury commits or confines a person in the exercise of that authority, knowing he is acting contrary to law.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes unlawful commitment or confinement by a person with authority` IF
        pj's `is in an office that gives him legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement or to keep persons in confinement`
    AND pj's `corruptly or with intent to cause injury to any person commits a person for trial or to confinement or keeps a person in confinement in the exercise of that authority`
    AND pj's `knows that in doing so he is acting contrary to law`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 221"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant intentionally omitting to apprehend a person charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence under Penal Code 1871 section 221
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A public servant legally bound to apprehend or confine a person charged with or liable to apprehension for an offence, who intentionally omits to apprehend him, suffers him to escape, or aids his escape.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant intentionally omitting to apprehend a person charged` IF
        pj's `is a public servant`
    AND pj's `is legally bound as a public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement a person charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence`
    AND pj's `intentionally omits to apprehend that person or intentionally suffers that person to escape or intentionally aids that person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 222"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant intentionally omitting to apprehend a person under sentence or lawfully committed under Penal Code 1871 section 222
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc The same omission, aid or sufferance where the person is under sentence of a court or lawfully committed to custody.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant intentionally omitting to apprehend a person under sentence` IF
        pj's `is a public servant`
    AND pj's `is legally bound as a public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement a person under sentence of a court of justice for an offence or lawfully committed to custody`
    AND pj's `intentionally omits to apprehend that person or intentionally suffers that person to escape or intentionally aids that person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 223"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant negligently suffering an escape from confinement under Penal Code 1871 section 223
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A public servant legally bound to keep in confinement a person charged with or convicted of an offence or lawfully committed, who negligently suffers him to escape.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant negligently suffering an escape` IF
        pj's `is a public servant`
    AND pj's `is legally bound as a public servant to keep in confinement a person charged with or convicted of an offence or lawfully committed to custody`
    AND pj's `negligently suffers that person to escape from confinement`

§§ `Sections 224 to 225C -- Resistance, escape, rescue, and the residual offences`

-- s 224 is the person's own apprehension or custody; s 225 is another's. ss 225A and
-- 225B are the residual cases "not provided for" in ss 221 to 223 and ss 224 to 225
-- or any other law; that residual character is a fact on each. s 225C is the
-- Code's last resort: a prohibited act or enjoined omission for which no special
-- punishment is provided, fined up to $2,000.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 224"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes resistance or obstruction to one's own lawful apprehension, or escape from custody, under Penal Code 1871 section 224
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Intentionally resisting or illegally obstructing one's own lawful apprehension for an offence charged or convicted, or escaping or attempting to escape from lawful custody for it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes resisting own apprehension or escaping` IF
    pj's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to his own lawful apprehension for an offence with which he is charged or of which he has been convicted or escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained for such an offence`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 225"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes resistance or obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another, or rescue, under Penal Code 1871 section 225
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Intentionally resisting or illegally obstructing another's lawful apprehension for an offence, or rescuing or attempting to rescue another from lawful custody for an offence. The five punishment tiers turn on the other person's offence or sentence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes resisting the apprehension of another or rescue` IF
    pj's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person for an offence or rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained for an offence`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 225A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant omitting to apprehend or suffering an escape in a case not otherwise provided for under Penal Code 1871 section 225A
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc A public servant legally bound to apprehend or confine a person in a case outside ss 221 to 223 and any other law, who intentionally or negligently omits to apprehend or suffers an escape.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant omitting to apprehend in a residual case` IF
        pj's `is a public servant`
    AND pj's `is legally bound as a public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement a person in a case not provided for in section 221 222 or 223 or in any other law for the time being in force`
    AND pj's `intentionally or negligently omits to apprehend that person or suffers him to escape from confinement`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 225B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes resistance, escape or rescue in a case not otherwise provided for under Penal Code 1871 section 225B
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc In a case outside ss 224 and 225 and any other law, intentionally resisting or obstructing any lawful apprehension, escaping from lawful custody, or rescuing another from it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes resistance escape or rescue in a residual case` IF
    pj's `in a case not provided for in section 224 or 225 or in any other law for the time being in force intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself or of another person or escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained or rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 225C"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes an offence against a law of Singapore for which no special punishment is provided under Penal Code 1871 section 225C
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Doing what a law in force in Singapore prohibits, or omitting what it enjoins, where the law provides no special punishment for it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a prohibited act with no special punishment provided` IF
        pj's `does anything which by a law in force in Singapore he is prohibited from doing or omits to do anything which he is so enjoined to do`
    AND pj's `no special punishment is provided by the law for the commission or omission`

§§ `Sections 228 and 229 -- Insult to a public servant sitting judicially, and personation of an assessor`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 228"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes intentional insult or interruption to a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding or conducting mediation under Penal Code 1871 section 228
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc Intentionally insulting or interrupting a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding or conducting a mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process under written law.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes insulting a public servant sitting judicially` IF
    pj's `intentionally offers insult or causes interruption to a public servant while sitting in any stage of a judicial proceeding or conducting a mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process under written law`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 229"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes personation of an assessor under Penal Code 1871 section 229
GIVEN pj IS A `Public Justice` @desc By personation or otherwise intentionally causing or knowingly suffering oneself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor when known not to be entitled, or knowingly serving after being so returned contrary to law.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes personation of an assessor` IF
        pj's `by personation or otherwise intentionally causes or knowingly suffers himself to be returned empanelled or sworn as an assessor in a case in which he knows that he is not entitled by law to be so returned empanelled or sworn`
    OR  pj's `knowing himself to have been returned empanelled or sworn as an assessor contrary to law voluntarily serves as such assessor`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an offence against evidence or information of an offence` IF
        (   `constitutes screening an offender by destroying evidence or false information` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes omission to give information of an offence` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes giving false information respecting an offence` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes destroying a document to prevent its production as evidence` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes perverting the course of justice` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes bribery of a witness` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes false personation in a suit or prosecution` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a false charge with intent to injure` (a's `public justice`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a fraud on forfeiture execution or a decree` IF
        (   `constitutes fraudulent removal of property to prevent its seizure` (a's `public justice`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes a fraudulent claim to property to prevent its seizure` (a's `public justice`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes fraudulently suffering a decree for a sum not due` (a's `public justice`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes fraudulently obtaining a decree for a sum not due` (a's `public justice`) (a's `fault`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes harbouring or screening an offender` IF
        (   `constitutes harbouring an offender` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes taking a gift to screen an offender` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes offering a gift to screen an offender` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes taking a gift to help recover stolen property` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes harbouring an escapee or a person ordered to be apprehended` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes harbouring robbers` (a's `public justice`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a public servant offence against public justice` IF
        (   `constitutes a public servant disobeying the law to save a person or property` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant framing an incorrect record to save a person or property` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant making a judicial order known to be contrary to law` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes unlawful commitment or confinement by a person with authority` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant intentionally omitting to apprehend a person charged` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant intentionally omitting to apprehend a person under sentence` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant negligently suffering an escape` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant omitting to apprehend in a residual case` (a's `public justice`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes resistance escape rescue or a residual contempt` IF
        (   `constitutes resisting own apprehension or escaping` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes resisting the apprehension of another or rescue` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes resistance escape or rescue in a residual case` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes a prohibited act with no special punishment provided` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes insulting a public servant sitting judicially` (a's `public justice`)
         OR `constitutes personation of an assessor` (a's `public justice`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
